('3be0914d-a34d-452c-b1de-69bd8d1a1d3f', 'Straight Hip Single Leg Curl (Stability Ball)', 'Legs', 'Stability Ball', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Straight Hip Single Leg Curl On Stability Ball targets your hamstrings through a controlled curling motion. Your calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The stability ball adds an instability challenge that activates more stabilizer muscles. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '90471201', '90471201-Straight-Hip-Single-Leg-Curl-on-Stability-Ball-(ma.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Position the stability ball as needed for Straight Hip Single Leg Curl On Stability Ball. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Straight Hip Single Leg Curl On Stability Ball', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'stability_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3bef0c22-1400-46bf-8c18-b5ebe60d6730', 'Frog Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '4611201', '04611201-Frog-Squat-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Works well for quads activation.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Frog Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3bfc433b-1ef1-4a78-abdb-c655a111e122', 'Decline Knee Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The decline position targets the lower portion of the muscles more intensely. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '65481201', '65481201-Decline-Knee-Raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Decline Knee Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Knee Raise', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Decline Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c00d849-7794-4082-a605-e658d31847cb', 'Seated Lateral Costal Breathing', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '99751201', '99751201-Sitting-Lateral-Costal-Breathing-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Lateral Costal Breathing. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'breathing', 'Seated Lateral Costal Breathing', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c021473-06e4-4ca2-a615-38872ae7a9ce', 'Squat And Reach - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this squatting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '80531201', '80531201-Alternating-Squat-and-Reach-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat And Reach - Alternating', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c1e8a1b-ca90-414c-a1fb-84f56d7e91c0', 'Seated Shoulder Press - Parallel Grip (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '4041201', '04041201-Dumbbell-Seated-Shoulder-Press-(parallel-grip)_Sho.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 86, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('3c274bc1-c5bd-4ce9-923a-8cb554b996ea', 'Hands To Feet Pada Hastasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your full body area and enhance overall flexibility. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '9531201', '09531201-Hands-to-Feet-Pada-Hastasana-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Hands To Feet Pada Hastasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Hands To Feet Pada Hastasana', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c33e024-8b0c-4e75-a57e-6e02290b92a9', 'Ed Feet Sit Up Stand', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Ed Feet Sit Up Stand, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '59291201', '59291201-Fixed-Feet-Sit-Up-Stand-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ed Feet Sit Up Stand. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Ed Feet Sit Up Stand', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c359332-66e0-48fe-a004-6a659e98bd69', 'Squat Hold Calf Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger calves with this targeted squatting exercise. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '45631201', '45631201-Dumbbell-Squat-Hold-Calf-Raise_Calves_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Squat Hold Calf Raise. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Squat Hold Calf Raise', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('3c44a31d-1028-40f9-8bbc-5b5af2015998', 'Side Toe Tap (Wall Supported)', 'Full Body', 'Wall', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Side Toe Tap Wall Supported is a lower body movement exercise that targets your full body. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '99091201', '99091201-Side-Toe-Tap-Wall-Supported-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Toe Tap Wall Supported. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 42, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Toe Tap Wall Supported', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c6545f4-8507-45f7-8472-f1dad52d0bd1', 'Chin Up - Close Grip (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. The biceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '23821201', '23821201-Close-Grip-Chin-Up-(female)_Back-FIX.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull yourself up, focusing on bicep and lat engagement. 3. Raise until chin is over the bar, lower with full control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Chin Up - Close Grip', 'Chin Up - Close Grip', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c8bdeab-bbd7-4b0e-ab73-5483ecf243f8', 'Seated Back Stretch (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Target your back with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '104611201', '104611201-Seated-Back-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Back Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 27, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Seated Back Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('3c8d0bd5-3066-48d1-89f7-3d1242d5c8de', 'Ring Skin The Cat (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Full Body', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your full body, the Ring Skin The Cat helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '106631201', '106631201-Ring-Skin-the-Cat-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Ring Skin The Cat. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Ring Skin The Cat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('3c8f754a-7b89-4a86-a366-fa32f100f2d8', 'Standing Lat Pulldown (Resistance Band)', 'Back', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '91441201', '91441201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Lat-Pulldown-(female)_Bac.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Lat Pulldown. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Standing Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50);
